erion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor must choose a version scheme to write the intent value the oracle table asserts, and could pick a different one than intended."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to Step 1 defining the version's source, e.g. 'each intent carries a schema-version integer sourced from a module constant' or 'the version is the observed binding revision from the snapshot'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether excluded/deferred plans carry a distinguishable reason (e.g. dependency-blocked vs. selection/filter vs. mode-cap/limit vs. tombstone/index-lag/move/link/partial-snapshot), aligning with the existing operation_outcome.Disposition vocabulary, so each AC outcome family has a deterministic, separately-assertable disposition.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ticket_plan.py:49-59 PlanDisposition = mutate/defer/noop only","operation_outcome.py:26-37 already distinguishes dependency_deferred, scope_deferred, safety_aborted, skipped","AC lines: 'Blocked prerequisites produce deferred plans', 'Selection, filter, mode cap, and global safety limits exclude work', 'tombstone, index-lag, move, link, partial-snapshot ... deterministic dispositions' — three distinct outcome families","Plan text names only 'deferred disposition' with no reason channel"],"finding":"The plan routes every excluded/blocked outcome through a single 'deferred disposition', but the acceptance criteria enumerate distinct outcome families — blocked prerequisites, selection/filter/mode-cap/limit exclusion, and tombstone/index-lag/move/impossible-link/partial-snapshot cases — that the existing apply-layer Disposition enum already distinguishes (dependency_deferred / scope_deferred / safety_aborted / skipped). The current PlanDisposition only has mutate/defer/noop. The plan does not say whether a deferred plan records WHY it deferred, so the 'deterministic dispositions' AC and the 'blocked prerequisites produce deferred plans' AC cannot be told apart from a limit-excluded or filtered plan.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9281247d99c69a4d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 & 4 / Acceptance Criteria (blocked-prereq deferral, pre-effect exclusion, ticket-sourced dispositions) / ticket_plan.py:49-59 PlanDisposition","norm_id":"nd817ae0fa1edae52","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A plan deferred because its create-prerequisite is blocked is indistinguishable from a plan excluded by max_changes or by selection, defeating the per-case 'deterministic disposition' tables","Held-out oracle tables that 'assert exact ... disposition values' cannot pin distinct dispositions if all excluded cases collapse to 'defer'"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify where an inter-ticket dependency EDGE is anchored (a pass-level dependency-edge set keyed by ticket identity vs. per-plan fields) and justify the choice, so create-before-link / parent-before-child edges have one unambiguous owner and blocked-prerequisite deferral is computable in the pure planner.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5175,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Encode create-before-link and parent-before-child prerequisites. A blocked prerequisite yields deferred disposition'","Plan: 'explicit inter-ticket dependencies to TicketPlan'","ticket_planner.py:110-126 builds one independent TicketPlan per Mutation.target with no cross-plan link","A create-before-link edge relates target A (the create) to target B (the link); a field on one frozen per-target plan cannot unambiguously represent a two-target edge"],"finding":"Create-before-link and parent-before-child prerequisites are INTER-ticket (cross-target) ordering constraints, but the plan anchors them as fields on the per-target TicketPlan, which plan_pass builds one-per-target with no cross-plan relationship. The plan does not say which of the two related plans owns the edge, nor does it weigh a structurally different alternative: a single pass-level dependency-edge set (on the Observation or as a companion return value) that the per-target plans reference by identity. A pass-level edge graph avoids duplicating/ambiguating an edge across two independent frozen plans and gives a single place to detect blocked prerequisites and compute deferral.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbcdec75602029af6","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 / Impacted sites — ticket_plan.py 'gains ... inter-ticket-dependency fields'; ticket_planner.py plan_pass (ticket_planner.py:110-126 groups by target only)","norm_id":"n2d910e38472ed322","priority":0.0825,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["local-9 must be created before REB-200's link mutation references it; where does the edge live — on local-9's plan, REB-200's plan, or both?","Parent P must precede child C; if only the child plan carries the dependency, discovering a blocked parent requires cross-plan lookup the plan never specifies"],"severity":"minor","sugge